# 2026-10-26 (manual update) — CacheArray sweep + ServerLog bulk write stress
# [FIX] jsplus-core CacheArray.java (D:\Working\JsPlus, rebuilt
#   jsplus-embed-6.1.0.jar -> LibHome\jsplus\default\):
#   * NEW sweepProcessed(int count): thread-safe head sweep. Rows persisted by
#     the filter thread are reclaimed instead of growing the cache forever.
#     Synchronized; touches only the head while concurrent add() always appends
#     at the tail, so new rows are never swept. O(n) single pass (removeAll),
#     avoids per-item ArrayList shifts.
#   * filter() loop now calls sweepProcessed(index) right after executeBatch
#     (i.e. after the batch is persisted) and keeps its local index in sync, so
#     the cache stays at ~one batch under sustained load. Safe under global
#     multi-thread access (ServerLog.webLogCacheArray is static/shared across
#     request threads). Other CacheArray.filter users are unaffected unless
#     they call sweep.
